@startuml
!include https://raw.githubusercontent.com/proveo-ca/identity/main/proveo.puml
skinparam noteTextAlignment left
' purpose: the chess user journey — every interaction from enter to result, as one path that reuses the primitive kit
' status: proposed 2026-09-17, not implemented; _spec/_plans/ is exempt from the SPEC-reference rule.
' would touch: not in this tree — no chess route, screen, or interaction map
'   exists under the sandbox checkout (measured 2026-09-17). Locate the owning
'   UI package before a covers: line can be honest.
'   the kit this path must use ......... _spec/_plans/chess-ui-primitives.puml
'   difficulty as a beat on this path .. _spec/_plans/chess-save-difficulty.puml
'   forfeit as a terminal verb ......... _spec/_plans/forfeit-as-loss.puml
'   export as a post-result verb ....... _spec/_plans/game-export-localstorage.puml
' Notes are capped at 5 lines x 50 columns; one idea per anchor.
'
' ── WHAT THE LINE ITEM SETTLES ─────────────────────────────────────────────
' "UI interactions/user journey" is the PATH, not a widget. Enter, pick a
' fight, play, finish, leave. Every verb the player can hit sits on that path
' or is declared out of scope. A pile of screens with no order is not a
' journey.
'
' ── WHAT IT DOES NOT SETTLE ────────────────────────────────────────────────
'   ranked vs casual vs tutorial as separate paths or one with gates
'   what happens on disconnect
'   whether analytics is on the path or a side door
'
' Salt wireframes belong in a sibling once the path is stable. This file owns
' why a row is gated; the wireframe would show what the gate draws.
title PLANNED — one chess path from enter to result;\norphan screens are not a journey

component "enter" as IN <<app>>
component "pick fight / difficulty" as PICK <<app>>
component "play" as PLAY <<app>>
component "result\nwin · loss · draw · forfeit" as END <<app>>
component "leave · export · rematch" as OUT <<app>>
component "**orphan screen**\nno way in, no way out" as ORPH <<error>>

IN ARROW_MAIN PICK
PICK ARROW_MAIN PLAY
PLAY ARROW_MAIN END
END ARROW_MAIN OUT
OUT ARROW_OPTIONAL IN
PLAY ARROW_ERROR ORPH : a dialog with no\npath edge
PICK ARROW_ERROR ORPH

note bottom of ORPH
  **A screen without a path edge should be
  removed, because a settings island that cannot
  return to play loses the match inside a menu.**
  Every surface names its backward and forward
  exits.
end note

note bottom of END
  **Result is one surface: victory, defeat, draw,
  and forfeit share the frame.** Four different
  end cards will fight the outcome enumeration the
  engine writes.
end note

note right of PICK
  **Difficulty is a required beat on this path
  before play begins.** Persisting that selection
  is a separate plan; this file only places the
  picker on the journey.
end note

legend bottom
  **The order to do it in**
  ==
  **1. Draw the live path.** Click through once. List every screen and every
  control that commits (move, forfeit, rematch, export). That list is the
  journey; missing verbs are bugs, extra screens are suspects.
  --
  **2. Put verbs on edges.** Enter → pick → play → result → leave. Difficulty
  save, forfeit, and export attach here; they do not get their own apps.
  ==
  **3. Wireframe after the path.** A salt sibling if row order is a contract.
  Until then, do not restyle primitives to paper over a missing edge.
  --
  **Left open**: tutorial as a branch or a separate path; disconnect;
  whether analytics is linked from result.
end legend
@enduml
